US-001 is done and `scripts/check.sh` passes all 13 steps, including the e2e lane. I closed bead p-atlas-layer-1qus.1.

- **State module:** `frontend/src/plugins/tags-atlas/atlasLayerState.ts` exports the `AtlasLayerState` type and the pure `next`, `prev` and `cycle`. It also has helpers to read, write and clear `data-atlas-layer` on `document.body`.
- **Boot wiring:** `frontend/src/app.ts` sets `data-atlas-layer="list"` on `<body>` at boot when `tags-atlas` is enabled.
- **Unit tests:** `frontend/test/atlasLayerState.test.ts` covers every transition and the attribute round trip.
- **E2E test:** `frontend/e2e/atlas-layer.test.ts` checks that `tags-atlas` is in `window.__PLUGINS__` and that the home page ends up in `list`.

Two places differ from the PRD:
- **E2E location:** the e2e file is `frontend/e2e/atlas-layer.test.ts`, not `e2e/atlas-layer.spec.ts`. `scripts/run-e2e.sh` only runs `frontend/e2e/*.test.ts`, so a file under `e2e/` would never run.
- **Plugin enable:** the e2e test has no enable step. `tags-atlas` is on by default, so a fresh e2e database already has it enabled.

I appended the notes to `.ralph-tui/progress.md`. I did not commit, as the workflow says.

